WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.059
ISIS will survive its losses in Iraq and Syria.

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:12.469
It is re-establishing a haven in Libya as
a base for coordinating attacks in Europe

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:15.369
and operations across Africa.

00:00:15.369 --> 00:00:19.840
ISIS operates freely in Libya’s interior
with access to lucrative smuggling and human

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:20.930
trafficking networks.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:26.269
The threat from ISIS in Libya to Europe, and
eventually the United States, will only grow

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:28.910
as ISIS shifts from Iraq and Syria.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:33.370
An ISIS unit in Libya facilitated the May
2017 Manchester bombing.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:38.590
ISIS has also challenged Tunisia—the lone
Arab Spring success—with attacks from Libya.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:42.290
The impact of military operations against
ISIS has been fleeting.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:47.250
It is recovering from the loss of Sirte, its
stronghold on the Libyan coast, to US-backed

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.960
forces in late 2016.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.650
The West cannot win against ISIS without defeating
it in Libya.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:57.080
Success in Libya requires ending its civil war,

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:01.480
which has allowed ISIS and other terrorist groups,  including al Qaeda,

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:06.380
to use the country as a base for planning and conducting attacks.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.040
What do you think is the best way to stop ISIS and al-Qaeda?

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.940
Let us know in your comments.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.040
Also, let us know what other topics you’d
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.520
and be sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

